{"name":"Spear Shaft","hex":"#885500","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spear","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long stick with a sharp tip used as a weapon for throwing or thrusting, or anything used to make a thrusting motion.","A soldier armed with such a weapon; a spearman."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pierce with a spear.","To penetrate or strike with, or as if with, any long narrow object; to make a thrusting motion that catches an object on the tip of a long device."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spear"},{"term":"shaft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The entire body of a long weapon, such as an arrow.","The long, narrow, central body of a spear, arrow, or javelin."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fuck over; to cause harm to, especially through deceit or treachery.","To equip with a shaft."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shaft"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spear","blocks":[{"text":"A spear is a polearm consisting of a shaft, usually of wood, with a pointed head. The head may be simply the sharpened end of the shaft itself, as is the case with fire hardened spears, or it may be made of a more durable material fastened to the shaft, such as bone, flint, obsidian, copper, bronze, iron, or steel. The most common design for hunting and/or warfare, since modern times has incorporated a metal spearhead shaped like a triangle, diamond, or leaf. The heads of fishing spears usually feature multiple sharp points, with or without barbs."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spear"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Hoplite_with_spear_from_Greco%E2%80%93Persian_Wars.png/250px-Hoplite_with_spear_from_Greco%E2%80%93Persian_Wars.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4d/Hoplite_with_spear_from_Greco%E2%80%93Persian_Wars.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Hoplite_with_spear_from_Greco%E2%80%93Persian_Wars.png/250px-Hoplite_with_spear_from_Greco%E2%80%93Persian_Wars.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spear-armed hoplite from Greco-Persian Wars","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHoplite_with_spear_from_Greco%E2%80%93Persian_Wars.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Clacton_Spear_02.jpg/500px-Clacton_Spear_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Clacton_Spear_02.jpg/1280px-Clacton_Spear_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Clacton_Spear_02.jpg/500px-Clacton_Spear_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClacton_Spear_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Sch%C3%B6ningen_wooden_artifacts_Lower_Palaeolithic.jpg/500px-Sch%C3%B6ningen_wooden_artifacts_Lower_Palaeolithic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Sch%C3%B6ningen_wooden_artifacts_Lower_Palaeolithic.jpg/1280px-Sch%C3%B6ningen_wooden_artifacts_Lower_Palaeolithic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Sch%C3%B6ningen_wooden_artifacts_Lower_Palaeolithic.jpg/500px-Sch%C3%B6ningen_wooden_artifacts_Lower_Palaeolithic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASch%C3%B6ningen_wooden_artifacts_Lower_Palaeolithic.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wiki